course: dictionary
lesson: 910
title: Words from history and science
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blacksmith is a person whose job is to make and repair things made of iron. Read the sentence first: «A blacksmith fits one horseshoe on each hoof, so every horse needs 4 horseshoes.» The clues are horseshoe and hoof, so a blacksmith works with iron for horses.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try: «A person who makes iron things fits one horseshoe on each hoof.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Many words come from history, science and old stories. The blacksmith appears in tales about villages, horses and knights. In science, heating metal makes it easier to shape, and a blacksmith uses that same idea.
fact: A blacksmith makes and repairs things made of iron, such as horseshoes, gates and tools.
fact: A blacksmith heats metal and then hammers it into shape.
fact: «The village blacksmith» is a common character in old stories about villages, horses and knights.
fact: «The blacksmith's forge» is the place where a blacksmith works.
fact: A horse needs 4 horseshoes, one for each hoof.
exercise: «A blacksmith fits one horseshoe on each hoof, so every horse needs 4 horseshoes.» What does a blacksmith do? | *Makes and repairs things made of iron, such as horseshoes | Grows crops in a field | Teaches children to read | Sells bread and cakes in a shop
exercise: In the sentence, what does a blacksmith fit on each hoof? | *horseshoe | horse | sentence | village
exercise: What does a blacksmith do to metal to shape it? | Wraps it in paper | Cuts it with scissors | *Heats it and hammers it into shape | Freezes it and paints it
test: Which place is the blacksmith's workshop, where the metal is heated? | The orchard | The library | *The forge | The stable
test: Which job uses heat and a hammer to shape iron? | Teacher | Gardener | *Blacksmith | Baker
exam: In an old story, «the village blacksmith» is busy all day. What is his job? | Driving the village bus | Teaching children to read | Selling flowers at the market | *Making and repairing iron things such as horseshoes and gates
